---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Records Handling Notice"
  kicker="Legal"
  heading="Records Handling Notice"
  lede="How PRC treats the records clients entrust to us. Effective August 2, 2026."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p>
        Records are the reason PRC exists, and we hold ourselves to the standard we teach.
        This notice states the protections that govern client records in PRC's care. It is part
        of every engagement, alongside the written scope.
      </p>

      <h2>The channel rule — read this first</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>PRC accepts sensitive records only through the secure channel agreed in your
        engagement</strong> — never through public website forms, the client portal, or ordinary
        unencrypted email. Our forms say so, and our staff will never ask you to send account
        numbers, government ID numbers, or medical details outside the agreed channel. If anyone
        claiming to be PRC does, stop and call us — that is how you know something is wrong.
      </p>

      <h2>Security commitments</h2>
      <p>Sensitive client records in PRC's care are protected by:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>A written information-security policy that every person with access signs.</li>
        <li>Role-based access — only the people working your engagement can reach your records.</li>
        <li>Multifactor authentication on systems that hold client records.</li>
        <li>Encryption in transit and at rest.</li>
        <li>Source-document preservation — your originals are never altered; work happens on copies.</li>
        <li>Audit logging and version history on records systems.</li>
        <li>Backups, with restore testing — a backup that has never been restored is a hope, not a backup.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Lifecycle commitments</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Retention and deletion schedules agreed in writing as part of your scope.</li>
        <li>Written incident-response procedures; if an incident affects your records, you will be told promptly and plainly.</li>
        <li>Security review of any vendor or tool that touches client records.</li>
        <li>Confidentiality obligations for everyone who works on your engagement.</li>
        <li>At offboarding: secure return or verified deletion of your records, at your direction, confirmed in writing.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What the client portal is — and is not</h2>
      <p>
        The client portal shows engagement status, milestones, and update notices. It deliberately
        holds no client documents, which means a portal code alone can never expose your records.
        Deliverables move through the engagement's agreed secure channel.
      </p>

      <h2>Your records are yours</h2>
      <p>
        PRC claims no ownership of client records — ever. You may direct return or deletion at any
        time, subject only to obligations in the written engagement, and we will confirm completion
        in writing.
      </p>

      <p style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        Questions about records handling: <strong>contact@paularecordscustodian.com</strong>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
